WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:07.490
That's what it must have sounded like when
Belgian special police forces stormed Dounia

00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:14.240
Depoorter's apartment on October 7th, 2018.

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:21.390
"They came in through here, forcefully pushed
me to the far end of the room.

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:25.960
When I opened the door, I was flung against
the piano and they twisted my hands behind

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:29.189
my back."

00:00:29.189 --> 00:00:38.500
The singer was sheltering two unregistered
Sudanese refugees at the time -- this is where

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:40.600
they slept.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:45.980
The Belgian police unit accused Depoorter
of people smuggling which left her speechless

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:51.800
"They told me: 'You are under arrest.

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:53.180
You no longer have any rights.

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:55.520
Be silent.'

00:00:55.520 --> 00:01:00.300
The whole situation was one long violent ordeal.

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:02.190
I was wearing my pajamas.

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:05.350
A female police officer dressed me.

00:01:05.350 --> 00:01:07.410
I couldn't even cry at that moment.

00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:09.920
Only later."

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:16.100
Her computer and telephone were seized to
check whether she was working with Belgian

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:18.300
people smugglers.

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:27.409
The 45-year-old was handcuffed, and led out
of her home - while her neighbors were watching.

00:01:27.409 --> 00:01:29.460
Where does human compassion end?

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:31.670
And where does people-smuggling begin?

00:01:31.670 --> 00:01:36.300
We meet a lawyer who defends many Belgians
who acted just like Dounia Depoorter, and

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:38.700
are now accused of people trafficking.

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:45.280
He says the authorities are abusing their
power.

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:50.329
It is simply unacceptable that the police
and public prosecutors are going after ordinary

00:01:50.329 --> 00:01:54.110
citizens, raiding their homes at 5 in the
morning.

00:01:54.110 --> 00:01:59.259
That is an abuse of power.

00:01:59.259 --> 00:02:05.120
There might be grounds to call in and question
citizens, which entails ringing their doorbell.

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:09.840
But not treating them as criminals.

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:15.510
This is Brussels' Park Maximilien, where refugees
flock who have no place to sleep, and don't

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:18.110
get regular meals.

00:02:18.110 --> 00:02:22.379
We want to know how their life has changed
now that many Belgian citizens are too scared

00:02:22.379 --> 00:02:29.270
to put them up for a few nights - because
of fear they are committing a crime.

00:02:29.270 --> 00:02:32.010
The refugees want to remain anonymous.

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:34.930
Josef is from Eritrea.

00:02:34.930 --> 00:02:38.599
He says he doesn't know where to sleep at
night, which makes braving the cold winter

00:02:38.599 --> 00:02:41.290
temperatures even harder.

00:02:41.290 --> 00:02:44.030
"How is your situation at the moment?

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:45.459
Where do you sleep at night?"

00:02:45.459 --> 00:02:46.840
"Here in the park."

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:48.989
"Do you have a blanket?"

00:02:48.989 --> 00:02:50.349
"Yes, I do.

00:02:50.349 --> 00:02:52.790
We all sleep here.

00:02:52.790 --> 00:02:57.379
My friends, too."

00:02:57.379 --> 00:03:01.790
The Belgian parliament is deeply divided over
how to treat migrants.

00:03:01.790 --> 00:03:05.840
Until recently, the right-wing nationalist
New Flemish Alliance party determined the

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:10.120
government’s tough stance on migrants, until
it quit the coalition in protest over the

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:11.970
UN migration pact.

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:14.060
What's their take on the current situation?

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:18.599
"I've got to do my duty...."

00:03:18.599 --> 00:03:23.040
We requested an interview, too, but never
received a reply.

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:29.060
Dounia Depoorter was forced to spend 24 hours
in solitary confinement, until a judge ruled

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:31.180
she was innocent.

00:03:31.180 --> 00:03:32.510
The ordeal has scarred her for life.

00:03:32.510 --> 00:03:38.220
It will take a long time for her to regain
trust in people so that some day she may feel

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:47.450
strong enough to again help others.

